# PDC Agent RHEL9 Rebase — Production Rollout Runbook

## Core safety principle

**Never deploy with a `latest` tag in prod.** Every build gets an immutable,
unique tag. The currently-running image and the previous known-good image
both stay cached on the host. Rollback is then just "point the Quadlet at
the old tag and restart" — no rebuild, no registry pull, no dependency on
anything external working. That's what makes it instant.

---

## 1. Pre-flight (do this before touching prod)

- [ ] Confirm you have a **known-good rollback target**: the exact image
      reference currently running in prod (e.g.
      `registry.internal/pdc-agent:v0.0.61-alpine-orig` or whatever the
      current stock image + tag is). Record it before you start:
      ```bash
      podman inspect pdc-agent --format '{{.ImageName}}'
      ```
- [ ] Confirm that image is present in **local Podman storage** on the prod
      host (not just the registry) — this is what makes rollback not depend
      on network/registry availability:
      ```bash
      podman images | grep pdc-agent
      ```
      If it's not local, pull it now, before the change window:
      ```bash
      podman pull <current-prod-image>:<current-tag>
      ```
- [ ] Change ticket / CAB approval, per your normal process.
- [ ] Maintenance window scheduled — even though PDC agent restarts are
      fast, any restart drops the SSH tunnel for a few seconds, which
      briefly interrupts any live Grafana Cloud query hitting a data
      source behind this agent.
- [ ] Notify anyone relying on dashboards/alerts fed through this PDC
      connection that a brief blip is expected.

---

## 2. Build with an immutable tag (staging/build host, NOT prod)

Never build directly on the prod host if you can avoid it — build on a
staging box or CI runner, validate there, then promote the *exact same
image digest* to prod. This guarantees "what you tested is what you ship."

```bash
cd ~/pdc-agent-rhel9

# Tag scheme: <upstream-pdc-version>-rhel9-<build-date>
# e.g. v0.0.61-rhel9-20260703
BUILD_TAG="v0.0.61-rhel9-$(date +%Y%m%d)"

podman build -t registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:${BUILD_TAG} -f Containerfile .
```

### Validate before it ever goes near prod

```bash
# Smoke test: binary runs, prints usage
podman run --rm --entrypoint /usr/bin/pdc \
  registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:${BUILD_TAG} -h

# Full connection test against a NON-PROD PDC network/stack if you have one.
# If you don't have a staging Grafana Cloud stack, at minimum run it
# standalone and confirm it reaches the auth handshake stage without erroring
# (do NOT point it at prod credentials for this step).
```

- [ ] Record the exact image digest, not just the tag, for your change
      record:
      ```bash
      podman inspect registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:${BUILD_TAG} --format '{{.Digest}}'
      ```

### Push to your internal registry

```bash
podman push registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:${BUILD_TAG}
```

---

## 3. Deploy to prod

### Pull the exact validated image onto the prod host

```bash
podman pull registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:${BUILD_TAG}
```

Confirm it's now sitting locally alongside the rollback image:

```bash
podman images | grep pdc-agent
```

You should see **both** the old known-good image and the new one. Do not
remove the old one yet — it stays until you've confirmed the new one is
stable (recommend: keep it for at least one full week post-deploy).

### Update the Quadlet with the pinned tag

```bash
sudo vi /etc/containers/systemd/pdc-agent.container
```

```ini
Image=registry.internal/pdc-agent-rhel9:v0.0.61-rhel9-20260703
```

(Never `:latest` — always the exact tag you validated.)

### Apply

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart pdc-agent.service
```

### Verify immediately

```bash
sudo journalctl -u pdc-agent -n 30 --no-pager
```

Look for the same success sequence every time:
```
msg="new client SSH certificate generated"
msg="Authenticated to private-datasource-connect-<cluster>.grafana.net ..."
msg="This is Grafana Private Datasource Connect!"
```

Then confirm from the Grafana Cloud side:
- **Connections → Private data source connect → Test agent connection**
- Confirm any dashboards/alerts that depend on data sources behind this
  agent are resolving normally (spot check 1-2 panels).

- [ ] Monitor for at least 15-30 minutes post-deploy before closing the
      change window. Watch for reconnect loops, auth failures, or
      unexpected restarts:
      ```bash
      sudo journalctl -u pdc-agent -f
      ```

---

## 4. Instant rollback procedure

If anything looks wrong — auth failures, crash loops, data sources not
resolving, anything — roll back immediately. Don't troubleshoot forward
under time pressure during a change window; roll back first, investigate
after.

```bash
sudo vi /etc/containers/systemd/pdc-agent.container
```

Change `Image=` back to the exact known-good reference you recorded in
step 1:

```ini
Image=<current-prod-image>:<current-tag>
```

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart pdc-agent.service
sudo journalctl -u pdc-agent -n 20 --no-pager
```

Because the rollback image is **already pulled and cached locally** (step
1 pre-flight), this restart happens in seconds with zero dependency on
registry availability, network egress, or anything outside the host
itself. That's the entire point of pinning tags and pre-pulling — the
rollback path has no external dependencies to fail.

- [ ] Confirm rollback success the same way as step 3 (journal logs +
      Grafana Cloud test connection).
- [ ] Document what went wrong before re-attempting the new image.

---

## 5. Post-deploy cleanup (only after the image has proven stable)

Once you're confident the new image is solid (recommend: 1+ week of
stable operation), you can prune the old rollback image if storage is a
concern:

```bash
podman images | grep pdc-agent
podman rmi <old-image>:<old-tag>
```

Don't rush this step. Keeping a known-good rollback image around costs a
few hundred MB of disk; not having one when you need it costs an incident.

---

## Summary checklist

| Step | Action |
|---|---|
| Pre-flight | Record current image, confirm it's cached locally |
| Build | Tag immutably (never `latest`), on staging not prod |
| Validate | Smoke test + connection test before promoting |
| Deploy | Pull exact validated tag onto prod, update Quadlet, restart |
| Verify | Check logs + Grafana Cloud connection test |
| Rollback (if needed) | Revert `Image=` tag to known-good, restart — seconds, no external deps |
| Cleanup | Prune old image only after proven stability window |
